# Endpoint Provenance

`∀ assistant turn closure: ¬sign_off` — who-did-what is endpoint provenance
(`seeded_by`, `caller_agent`, `from_agent`, execution records, model strings),
never a signed or asserted identity.

`∀ boot/dispatch prompt: ¬assert_identity_at_agent` — "you are X" banned;
frame duty as seat/function, not persona.

`∀ prose/bus/skills: ¬personal_name(Claude)` — never address or narrate the
model as a person named Claude. Naming preference order (best → worst):
`web-anthropic` → `anthropic` → `claude.ai` (**least preferred** — product
label only when the third-party UI itself is the subject). Agent-bus
`from`/`to` use endpoint addresses (`web-anthropic`, `cursor`), never
`claude` as a name. Model artifact strings (`claude-opus-…`) and permanent
runtime aliases (`claude-web` → `web-anthropic`) remain.

**Bus subjects / WIP / cover letters (recurrence class — friction 24421):**
✗ `chain Claude` · `Claude final` · `push Claude` · `Claude already executed`
✓ `chain to web-anthropic` · `web-anthropic final` · `push web-anthropic`
`claude.ai` only when the third-party product UI itself is the subject
(e.g. Customize Skills upload), never as a seat shorthand.

Doctrine: `decision:identity-doctrine-endpoint-provenance`.
The former `agent_skill:agent-identity-signoff` playbook is retired.
